[font size="5"][font color="#d6ad68"][b][Client Mod] Keybinder 0.7.5[/b][/font][/font]

[font size="3"][b]Put the action queue on either side of the screen[/b][/font]

[hr]

Hello, SKLOTOPOLIS!

Keybinder 0.7.5 is ready for testing.

This small interface update lets you place the compact Queue Monitor on either the right or left edge of the screen. Its complete layout mirrors automatically, including the drawer direction, lamps, text, border, and header arrow.

[hr]

[font size="4"][font color="#d6ad68"][b]What is new in 0.7.5?[/b][/font][/font]

[font size="3"][font color="#d6ad68"][b]Left or right screen edge[/b][/font][/font]

Open the Keybinder window and use [b]Queue monitor → Right edge / Left edge[/b] beside the action queue limit. The choice takes effect immediately and is saved for the next launch.

On the left edge the panel is fully mirrored:

[ul][li]the panel opens toward the center of the screen;[/li][li]the lamp and arrow column moves to the panel's right side;[/li][li]the arrow reverses its open and close directions;[/li][li]action, Tool, and Target text is right-aligned beside the lamps;[/li][li]the inner border moves to the correct side.[/li][/ul]

[font size="3"][font color="#d6ad68"][b]Expanded header[/b][/font][/font]

When the panel is open, the space above the action rows now displays the localized [b]Queue monitor[/b] title. The collapsed strip remains minimal and shows only its direction arrow and Build Menu-style queue lamps.

[font size="3"][font color="#d6ad68"][b]Compatibility[/b][/font][/font]

[ul][li]The new setting is localized in English, Brazilian Portuguese, and German.[/li][li]Existing installations default to the original right-edge layout.[/li][li]Saved keybinds remain compatible with 0.7.4.[/li][/ul]

[hr]

[font size="4"][font color="#d6ad68"][b]Installation and upgrade[/b][/font][/font]

[ol][li]Disable the old Custom Actions, Improved Improve, and i2improve client mods.[/li][li]Download Keybinder 0.7.5: [a href="https://github.com/chamomilo/wurm-keybinder/releases/tag/v0.7.5"]Download Keybinder 0.7.5 from GitHub[/a][/li][li]Extract keybinder-0.7.5.zip into your Wurm Unlimited client directory, as usual for Ago's Client Mod Launcher.[/li][li]When upgrading, simply overwrite the existing Keybinder files. Your managed keybinds are stored separately and are not replaced by the archive.[/li][li]Start the game. If the KB icon is not visible, enable Keybinder in HUD Settings.[/li][/ol]

[hr]

Keybinder is a keybind manager, not an unattended automation or scripting system. It sends ordinary Wurm actions while respecting your character's action queue.

If you find a bug or have another idea, please reply here and include the relevant Event log. Enable Debug logging when possible.

Cheers!

Chamomilo
